Z||000000||Wannabe||05-24-2001||11:41 AM||||Anybody know what the chanber volume is for these heads? I would like to figure out what the compression ratio would work out to if these heads were bolted to a 2.8 Fiero block with the stock 8.9:1 pistons. I'm aware of the the intake manifold incompatibilty - that will be dealt with - just wondering about chanber volume.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Black88GT||05-24-2001||02:16 PM||||I asked my friend and he said stock approx 28cc.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Steve Normington||05-24-2001||03:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Wannabe:<BR>I'm aware of the the intake manifold incompatibilty - that will be dealt with - <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Are you also aware of the bracket bolt pattern incompatibility? IE, the bolts in the side of the head where the dogbone / alternator / compressor brackets go are not the same pattern as the Fiero heads.<P><P>------------------<BR>I don't car if my next Fiero is a 2M Hamster, I'm not swapping the engine.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dave Gunsul||05-24-2001||09:30 PM||||You should also be aware that if you use these heads and convert to the Barretta,Z24,etc intake combo (which is less efficient) you will also have to change to the DIS ignition system since the upper plenum of the cars listed above will hit the<BR>Fieros distributor.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||13
